ext":"+"},{"text":"AI-Assisted Research"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Environmental Policy Internship"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Research Portfolio"}]}]},{"heading":"Best Overall Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["LL.B.","Environmental Law","Constitutional & Administrative Law","Environmental/Climate Knowledge","Public Policy","Research Methodology","Policy Writing","Data Analysis + GIS","Environmental Policy Internship","Research Assistant","Policy Analyst","Environmental Policy Researcher","Senior Policy Advisor / Policy Lead"]},{"type":"p","text":"For this career, the strongest profile is law + environmental knowledge + public-policy research + data skills. The graduate should be able to take an environmental problem, investigate the evidence, understand the existing legal framework, evaluate competing policy options, analyze stakeholder and economic impacts, and produce a concise, evidence-backed recommendation that policymakers or institutions can actually use."}]}]}